ng selections. Then I'm adding a test case with sample input to verify the solution works correctly. The user didn't specify what kind of refactoring they wanted, so I should probably ask what improvements they're looking for rather than assume.\n\nActually, looking at the code structure, I think introducing an `Activity` class would be a good next step—it would replace the parallel arrays with a proper data model and eliminate the magic index access. I'll go with records since they're clean and modern, though a static nested class would work too if an older Java version is being used.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":27960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89d1c982-f568-4aa7-9bb9-d37e15a707ec","uuid":"1f309ca1-8358-4158-85de-183b0d2a23e4","request_id":"req_011CcERrDh9yTa5Ekw6SX3k4"}
